notes:
Local communities are directly affected by decisions concerning land, water, forests, mining, conservation and development projects.

Participation helps to:
🔹 identify local needs;
🔹 reduce grievances;
🔹 improve acceptance of decisions;
🔹 protect livelihoods;
🔹 distribute benefits more fairly;
🔹 strengthen resource management.

⭐ Inclusive decision-making is essential for peaceful and sustainable resource use.

🏛️ Formal system → based mainly on written laws, courts and official institutions.

🌿 Indigenous system → based mainly on customs, elders, community relationships and traditional institutions.

Indigenous mechanisms can be valuable because they:
🔹 are locally accessible;
🔹 use community knowledge;
🔹 emphasize reconciliation;
🔹 consider long-term social relationships;
🔹 may produce mutually acceptable outcomes.

⚠️ Their practices vary between communities and may not have uniform application.
